gamerule.ability_scaling.name=Ability Scaling
gamerule.ability_scaling.desc=How much of a size change carries over to speed, reach and jump, in percent. 100 makes a 2x player move, reach and jump 2x as far; 0 changes only the body.
gamerule.do_size_griefing.name=Size Griefing
gamerule.do_size_griefing.desc=If enabled, size affects the world: big players trample farmland, crack ice, flatten grass where they land and wreck snow layers, small players never trample farmland, and a big enough body can tread on a small enough one.
gamerule.size_trample_players.name=Size Trample Players
gamerule.size_trample_players.desc=If enabled, a player small enough to be underfoot can be trodden on by a much bigger player or mob. Disabled, players are never crushed whatever the size gap; mobs still are. Only has an effect while Size Griefing is on.
gamerule.do_size_stomp_sounds.name=Size Stomp Sounds
gamerule.do_size_stomp_sounds.desc=If enabled, a very large player's footfalls are loud enough to hear across a valley. Off by default: the noise is a fine entrance and tiresome by the hundredth step.
gamerule.do_size_water_displacement.name=Size Water Displacement
gamerule.do_size_water_displacement.desc=If enabled, a very large player parts shallow water as they wade through it. Its own setting because it moves blocks every tick a giant is in the water, which a busy server may not want to pay for.
gamerule.starting_size.name=Starting Size
gamerule.starting_size.desc=The size a player is the first time they join this world. Random draws a different size for each new player, between 0.4x and 2.5x. Only applies to players the world has no size on record for; /scaling set overrides it afterwards.
gamerule.starting_size.value.random=Random
gamerule.starting_size.value.x0_4=0.4x
gamerule.starting_size.value.x0_5=0.5x
gamerule.starting_size.value.x0_66=0.66x
gamerule.starting_size.value.x0_75=0.75x
gamerule.starting_size.value.normal=Normal
gamerule.starting_size.value.x1_25=1.25x
gamerule.starting_size.value.x1_5=1.5x
gamerule.starting_size.value.x2=2x
gamerule.starting_size.value.x2_5=2.5x
gamerule.do_size_drag.name=Size Drag
gamerule.do_size_drag.desc=If enabled, terrain is harder going at some sizes: undergrowth and snow hold a small player back, and a leaf canopy holds a big one back. Disabled, ground cover costs everybody the same and only the body's own speed differs. Does not stop a large player breaking the trees they walk through -- that is Size Griefing.
gamerule.do_size_scaled_cursor.name=Size Scaled Cursor
gamerule.do_size_scaled_cursor.desc=If enabled, a player twice normal size or more can mine and place a square of blocks at once, as wide as they are: 2x2 at 2x, 3x3 at 3x. It costs the full price either way -- the mining takes as long, the tool wears by as many points and the blocks cost as many items -- so it changes how much of a job happens per swing and nothing else. Off by default, and each player still has to switch it on with their own key.
